    <item>
      <title>Overview</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/docs/overview/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 03 Jan 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/docs/overview/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the &lt;strong&gt;ETLX documentation&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This guide explains &lt;strong&gt;what ETLX is&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;why it exists&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;how to think about it&lt;/strong&gt; before diving into pipelines, configuration, and execution details.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you are looking for a fast way to get started, jump directly to the &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/docs/docs/quickstart/&#34;&gt;Quickstart&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-etlx&#34;&gt;What is ETLX? &lt;a href=&#34;#what-is-etlx&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ETLX&lt;/strong&gt; is an &lt;strong&gt;open-source, developer-first ETL framework&lt;/strong&gt; designed to make data pipelines:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simpler&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More transparent&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Easier to reason about&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fully observable and reproducible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Instead of relying on heavyweight orchestration platforms or opaque runtime behavior, ETLX embraces a &lt;strong&gt;declarative, metadata-first approach&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Quickstart</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/docs/quickstart/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 08 Jun 2025 19:25:22 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/docs/quickstart/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;-requirements&#34;&gt;✅ Requirements &lt;a href=&#34;#-requirements&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Depending on how you install ETLX:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;minimum&#34;&gt;Minimum &lt;a href=&#34;#minimum&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Linux, macOS, or Windows&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DuckDB-compatible environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;optional-for-building-from-source&#34;&gt;Optional (for building from source) &lt;a href=&#34;#optional-for-building-from-source&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go ≥ 1.21&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;git&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-installation&#34;&gt;📦 Installation &lt;a href=&#34;#-installation&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Choose &lt;strong&gt;one&lt;/strong&gt; of the following options.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;option-1-precompiled-binary-recommended&#34;&gt;Option 1: Precompiled Binary (Recommended) &lt;a href=&#34;#option-1-precompiled-binary-recommended&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Download the latest release for your OS from:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;👉 &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/realdatadriven/etlx/releases&#34; rel=&#34;external&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;https://github.com/realdatadriven/etlx/releases&lt;svg width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill=&#34;currentColor&#34; d=&#34;M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Notifications</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/docs/features/notify/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/docs/features/notify/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;notifications&#34;&gt;Notifications &lt;a href=&#34;#notifications&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;NOTIFY&lt;/code&gt; section enables sending notifications (e.g., email via SMTP) with dynamic templates populated from SQL query results. This is useful for monitoring ETL processes and sending status reports.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;why-use-notify&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Use NOTIFY?&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#why-use-notify&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;✅ &lt;strong&gt;Real-time updates on ETL status&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;✅ &lt;strong&gt;Customizable email templates with dynamic content&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;✅ &lt;strong&gt;Supports attachments for automated reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;✅ &lt;strong&gt;Ensures visibility into ETL success or failure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;example-sending-etl-status-via-email&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example: Sending ETL Status via Email&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#example-sending-etl-status-via-email&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This example sends an email &lt;strong&gt;after an ETL process completes&lt;/strong&gt;, using &lt;strong&gt;log data from the database&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Requires</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/docs/features/require/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 01:04:15 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/docs/features/require/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;requires&#34;&gt;Requires &lt;a href=&#34;#requires&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;REQUIRES&lt;/code&gt; section in the ETL configuration allows you to load dependencies from external Markdown configurations. These dependencies can either be loaded from file paths or dynamically through queries. This feature promotes modularity and reusability by enabling you to define reusable parts of the configuration in separate files or queries.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;loading-structure&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Loading Structure&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#loading-structure&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;material-icons align-middle&#34;&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Metadata&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;REQUIRES&lt;/code&gt; section includes metadata describing its purpose and activation status.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Loading Options&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
